OL,3,GNEWSAPavement driving defended as roads
OL,4,Aunder pressure
OL,5,
OL,6,FCommittee President Adrian Gabriel said
OL,7,Fmany of the island's roads were
OL,8,F"historic, narrow, and constrained" by
OL,9,Fbuildings, walls and limited pavement
OL,10,Fspace; and, in some locations, vehicles
OL,11,Fcould not pass each other without one
OL,12,Fmounting the footpath.
